<title>SINGAPORE: Singatronics pares losses in 1996.</title>
<headline>Singatronics pares losses in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>			 (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net loss				1.48   vs    5.07</p>
<p>    Dividend (pct)			nil    vs    2.00</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents, loss)	   6.00   vs    2.70  (loss)</p>
<p>    Turnover			     42.90   vs   91.23</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest     3.73   vs    1.92</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		  3.03   vs    1.91</p>
<p>    Depreciation (expense)	    3.81   vs    5.48</p>
<p>    Profits from associates	   0.08   vs    0.39</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit	     (gain) 0.85   vs    4.11 (loss)</p>
<p>    Tax				     1.06   vs    0.18 (gain)</p>
<p>    Minorities		   (loss) 1.35   vs    1.52 (loss)</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries	    (loss) 6.05   vs    5.01 (gain)</p>
<p>Note - Singatronics Ltd said it incurred an extraordinary loss of S$6.09 million due to closure of unprofitable contract manufacturing operations in Batam and Singapore. Group turnover fell 53 percent to S$42.9 million due to these shutdowns.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 870 3080)</p>
</text>
